From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:59:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox: a jail that hides the host is named for its
 project

Operator ask of 2026-11-23 (item 5): every jail was `ai-sandbox`, so two
projects looked like the same machine and both said "sandbox". The decision
(2026-11-24): a stable name per project that looks like an ordinary
machine's -- `desktop-` and six lowercase letters or digits.

jail_hostname.rs hashes (SHA-256) a secret kept on this machine with the
project's canonical root. The name is the same on every start of the
project and says nothing about its path: without the secret, nobody can
tell which folder a name belongs to, or that two names are this machine's.
The secret is 32 bytes from /dev/urandom in
<data dir>/agent_sandbox/hostname.key (0600, directory 0700), made on first
use with create_new so two Zeos racing keep one file; a file of another size
is refused rather than replaced, since replacing it would rename every
project. sha2 rather than std's hasher: its output may change between Rust
releases, and a name must not change with the toolchain.

The launch passes `--hostname <name>` when the project hides the host
(mask_host) and the installed ai-jail lists the option (probe
supports_hostname, ai-jail 3.5.0-r6). ai-jail gives the name to the UTS
namespace, /etc/hosts, /etc/hostname and, under Hide the Kernel, uname(2),
so the answers agree. An older ai-jail starts as before, as `ai-sandbox` --
it hides as much, only less individually -- and an unreadable secret skips
the option the same way; both are logged. The secret's path reaches the
launch through LaunchEnv, so tests keep it in their fixture. The Hide the
Host note says the jail gets a host name of its own.

Logs: agent_sandbox event=hostname_secret_created, event=hostname_skipped
reason=unsupported|secret.

Tests: jail_hostname_tests.rs -- the name is one DNS label of the chosen
shape, stable per project and different across projects and secrets; the
secret is made once, owner-only, and kept; a damaged secret is never replaced
and skips the option; and, through the launch, a hidden-host jail is named
and keeps its name, while an older ai-jail or a shown host gets no option and
no secret.
---

